{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779462280,"nonce":"8Dx1o9IPMbofiywnDPR7inC1GCc=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDG_oIA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/155","origin":"github"},"title":"urdf: consolidate measured SBG + CUAV geometry (supersedes #110)","message":"## Summary\n\nConsolidate all measured / device-configured geometry uncovered during the\n2026-05-21 deployment + 2026-05-22 bag review into the BizzyBoat URDF\n(`bizzyboat_project11/urdf/bizzyboat.urdf.xacro`). The data was collected\nacross 2026-04-22 (tape measurements on the boat), 2026-05-22 (SBG flash\nphotos on mercat), and the 2026-05-21 bag — but never landed in the URDF.\nWithout it, the position/attitude comparisons #150 topic 1 needs to do for\n#138 closure don't have a clean geometric reference.\n\nSupersedes #110 (the original SBG-INS / GNSS-antenna gap issue) — that one\nhas the 2026-04-29 evidence; this one folds in the new measurements + adds\nCUAV refinement.\n\n## What needs to land in the URDF\n\n### 1. SBG Ellipse-D INS — new link\n\n- **Position from base_link**: `(−0.577, 0.000, +0.029) m` REP-103 FLU\n  (measured 2026-04-22 — see `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md:580`).\n- **Orientation**: 180° roll about X. SBG axis triad: X-fwd, Y-stbd, Z-into-page (FRD body frame); vessel uses REP-103 FLU. URDF joint rpy = `(π, 0, 0)`.\n- Suggested link name: `bizzy/sbg_imu`. New static joint from `base_link`.\n\n### 2. SBG Trimble GNSS antennas — two new links\n\nBoth on the existing center rail (z ≈ 0.89 m, same rail as CUAV antennas):\n\n| Antenna | x (m) | y (m) | z (m) | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Forward Trimble | **+0.990** | 0.000 | ~0.89 + phase-center δ | Tape: 15.5 cm fwd of fwd CUAV |\n| Aft Trimble | **−1.065** | 0.000 | ~0.89 + phase-center δ | Tape: 23 cm aft of aft CUAV |\n\nBaseline 2.055 m (tape) — matches SBG flash config (1.567 − (−0.488) = 2.055 m).\n\nSuggested link names: `bizzy/sbg_gnss_forward`, `bizzy/sbg_gnss_aft`.\n\n### 3. CUAV C-RTK 2HP GNSS antennas — already modeled, but verify Z\n\nCurrently in `bizzyboat.urdf.xacro:162-166`:\n- `bizzy/gnss_forward` at `(+0.835, 0, +0.89)` m\n- `bizzy/gnss_aft` at `(−0.835, 0, +0.89)` m\n\nThe X positions are tape-measured. The Z = 0.89 m is \"assumed rail-top per existing reference geometry\" — not independently measured. Worth a tape verification once the SBG antennas are also being measured for Z. Phase-center δ may differ between Trimble and CUAV pucks; capture both.\n\n### 4. SBG-device-config cross-check (no URDF change, just document)\n\nThe SBG flash config (photos in `~/sbg/2026-05-22_config/`) records the same lever arms in SBG FRD body frame:\n\n| Field | SBG flash | Install-log equivalent in REP-103 FLU |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vehicle Center of Rotations (CoR) lever arm | `(0.58, 0.00, 0.03) m` FRD | base_link is at `(+0.577, 0, −0.029)` m from SBG IMU |\n| Output Monitoring Point #1 | `(0.577, 0.000, 0.029) m` FRD, location = \"Center of Rotation\" | Output deported to base_link |\n| ANT1 (primary, aft) lever arm from IMU | `(−0.488, 0, −0.881) m` FRD | aft Trimble is at `(−1.065, 0, +0.910)` from base_link |\n| ANT2 (secondary, fwd) lever arm from IMU | `(+1.567, 0, −0.881) m` FRD | fwd Trimble is at `(+0.990, 0, +0.910)` from base_link |\n\nSo **the device-side intent is \"report at base_link\"**. Whether the SBG firmware actually deports `ekf_nav` to the Output Monitoring Point (or only deports `ship_motion`) is the open question that #150 topic 1 bag analysis is checking against the validated 12:34:39 → 14:33:42 in-water window.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\n- This issue is URDF + measurement-documentation only.\n- Lever-arm correction of the position streams to base_link is downstream (covered by #138 + the chain validation in #150 topic 1).\n- If the bag analysis from #150 topic 1 reveals a residual offset between SBG and mavros at base_link, that's a config or chain bug to investigate separately — not part of this URDF work.\n\n## Open unknowns\n\n(From `hydro_payload_install_log.md:509-516, 551-557`)\n\n- Exact Trimble model (only \"GNSS/MSK\" visible on case) — needed for phase-center datasheet\n- Phase-center height above mount base for both Trimble and CUAV pucks\n- IMU sensing-element offset from SBG case exterior — needed to place IMU origin precisely\n- Independent tape verification that y = 0 for both Trimbles\n- SBG case Z = +0.005 m bottom-of-case (line 528) is plate-thickness measurement, not IMU origin\n\nThese can be captured as `[EST]` / `[MEAS rough]` annotations in the URDF and refined later.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter URDF lands:\n\n- `ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames` shows `bizzy/sbg_imu`, `bizzy/sbg_gnss_forward`, `bizzy/sbg_gnss_aft` present alongside existing `bizzy/imu`, `bizzy/gnss_forward`, `bizzy/gnss_aft`.\n- Re-run #150 topic 1 SBG-vs-mavros position diff using TF-projected positions; the body-frame residual should drop toward GPS-CEP (sub-decimeter) modulo whatever ekf_nav-deport question turns out to be.\n\n## References\n\n- 2026-04-22 measurements: `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md:472-583`\n- 2026-05-22 SBG flash photos: `~/sbg/2026-05-22_config/PXL_20260522_*.jpg`\n- 2026-05-21 bag (in-water window 12:34:39 → 14:33:42 EDT): `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-05-21T*/`, extracted to `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21_deployment.db`\n- gabby §11 SBG-vs-mavros comparison: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-21_gabby_logs.md:757-` \n- Existing CUAV antennas in URDF: `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/bizzyboat.urdf.xacro:162-166`\n\nSupersedes #110.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}